-- 0172: Jamhara weak-letter bin re-keyed by headword (0151's group-head rule had filed 17,129 blocks under خوو / يهيه / راي).
-- 1,736 blocks placed with high confidence (headword → exactly one root; body agrees, or the group head's letters fit);
-- method 'jamhara_headword'. 15,393 verse lines, headers and unclear blocks stay where they were. Read-checked: 29/30
-- right in the agent's sample, 29/30 in the main session's (وَكَرَى was put under كري — fixed below to وكر).
-- jam_rekey: Jamhara (ibn_durayd_jamharat_lugha) blocks that AL 0151 re-keyed by the "group head" rule to the
-- wrong root, re-keyed by their own first headword. Touches ar_ling_lexicon_block_rekey ONLY (never
-- ar_ling_lexicon_block — FTS triggers). Every statement is guarded: method = 'jamhara_group_head' AND the old
-- root_norm_canonical AND an explicit block_id list, so 'manual' rows (0170) and anything already changed are left alone.
--
-- What was wrong (0151): in the weak-letter bin (ingested root_norm 'حيي', entry re_jam_bba2a268773c7a27, printed
-- p.540) every block after the bin's last group head «[خوو]» (seq 3628) inherited خوو — 16,935 rows, i.e. the whole
-- rest of the book from حرف الدال on. In 'نيني' (re_jam_2e809ed13482c276, p.189) 116 blocks after «[يهيه]» inherited
-- يهيه (they are the reduplicated بأبأ/تأتأ/دأدأ … chapters), and 78 blocks under the merged head «[رَأْي رويريا]»
-- were all put under راي though part are روي. The حيي runs → خلف (102, p.540) and → خلل (93, p.67; 2, p.540) were read
-- and are right (their blocks are خلف / خلل words) — not touched.
--
-- How each block's root was found:
--   1. first headword = first content word of the block's first sentence (skipping و/ف/ال, يقال/قال …, «رجل/بنو X»),
--      tashkīl stripped, hamza seats → ا, ى → ي, ة → ه. Verse lines, headers, «قال الشاعر:» intros and
--      continuations (أي …, وهو …, إنما …) have no headword and are left unchanged.
--   2. headword → root via ar_ling_root_lemma (lemma_text_bare and coalesce(lemma_text_canonical, lemma_text), live rows)
--      + ar_ling_roots; weak/hamzated spellings collapsed via ar_ling_root_lexicon_key (عفا → عفو). Only a root that is
--      a lookup key of itself is used, so the block stays visible in ar_ling_root_lexicon_block_v.
--   3. accepted only if the headword maps to exactly ONE root (or to one root that is also a permutation of the
--      edition's group head «(درز)» above it), AND
--        - the other headwords in the body (words before a «:», sentences opening «وال…») agree by strict majority, or
--        - there are none, and the root is a permutation of the group head above it (or, in the 4/5-letter
--          chapters, the headword is itself the 4/5-letter root).
--
-- Counts (of 17,129 rows: 16,935 خوو + 116 يهيه + 78 راي):
--   resolved     1736  → re-keyed below (خوو 1718, يهيه 13, راي→روي/ضفندد 5); 1360 (old,new) groups
--   confirmed       4  (headword confirms the current root راي — not touched)
--   ambiguous    3517  (headword maps to 2+ roots, body disagrees, or no corroboration) — not touched
--   unresolved  11872  (verse lines, headers, quotation intros, continuations, headword not in the lemma map) — not touched
-- Eye check: 30 random resolved blocks read — 29 right, 1 arguable (المَرْو → مري, as the lemma table files مَرْو;
-- Lane/Lisān file it under مرو). See jam_rekey.md.
-- Generated 2026-10-07 from a read of the live AL D1. Not applied.

